Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:40:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] fix(TDA): bound the unrolling of recursive types

Transparent types are trees, so a recursive type such as
struct node { int key; struct node *next; } is unrolled, and every iteration
of the fixed-point loop of the analysis can unroll it once more: on programs
with linked lists or trees EDDI never terminated. The submodule now points to
a version of TypeDeductionAnalysis that keeps opaque the pointers to a struct
already on the path from the root of the type (and bounds the nesting depth).
The patch for TypeDeductionAnalysis is in aspis-integration/patches/tda/.
---
 libs/TypeDeductionAnalysis | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/TypeDeductionAnalysis b/libs/TypeDeductionAnalysis
index f9f6e44..ea654af 160000
--- a/libs/TypeDeductionAnalysis
+++ b/libs/TypeDeductionAnalysis
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit f9f6e4450ae8d1bf7ad398c0541cb39211eb3075
+Subproject commit ea654af91c371d8479fc2ad6e8520b1d2335ca9f
